  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1248 PM CDT Sun Jul 12 2026\n\nWe still have a few showers rotating through eastern portions \nof the area this afternoon as an upper disturbance continues \nits eastward movement. This activity will wane through the\nevening with dry conditions overnight. \n\nThe upper disturbance will drift southeast into the Tennessee \nValley into Monday with ridging expanding across the northern \nplains. Overall much quieter weather is expected with the \nexception of a few isolated to widely scattered rain chances \nduring the afternoon hours. Highs in the mid 80s through \nWednesday will climb into the upper 80s to near 90 degrees by \nlate week.",
